## 2. Mix bus refit (12 October 2026)

Three bus candidates were built in each of two passes and the best by the mix critic was kept (all logged in `/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-motion-design/docs/build/MI-assemble-logs/build-V037.log`):

| Version | Bus | mix tfBands |
|---|---|---|
| V_035 | eq and compressor refit, then per-stem trims, then eq refit again (last state kept) | 98.842 |
| V_036 | best of the refit bus and the trimmed bus with loudness re-matched | 98.839 |
| **V_037** | **trims plus the bus output gain as a coordinate (pass 1 kept)** | **99.064** |

Kept bus of V_037: stem trims bass -1.5 dB, other -1.0 dB, drums -0.25 dB, vocals 0; per-section eq measured by `resynth.measure_eq`; the compressor grid chose no compression (threshold 100 dB over the loudness, ratio 1.5, inactive); output gain 1.45 dB; limiter ceiling -1.05 dBTP. (12 October 2026)

Diagnosis that redirected V_036 to V_037: the reference peaks at +0.99 dBTP while our delivery ceiling is -1.05 dBTP, so matching -9.02 LUFS pushes about 2.4 LU into the limiter (our V_036 mix measures -6.89 LUFS without it). A probe of the V_036 bus gain gave -3 dB 98.73, -2 dB 99.01, -1.5 dB 99.03, -1 dB 99.00, 0 dB 98.84, +0.5 dB 98.73: the critic prefers a less limited, slightly quieter mix. (12 October 2026)

