## 5. What still blocks 99 (12 October 2026)

- **other, 98.463** is the only stem under 99, and it plateaued in its own iteration (MI-other). Its error is scatter, not a level bias (missing 19.4 percent, extra 19.1 percent; fixing either alone gives 99.0); the heaviest groups are 120 to 500 Hz (32 percent of the error, 2.88 dB mean) and 30 to 120 Hz (18.5 percent, 4.80 dB), and 70 percent of the error sits on onset frames. Next methods: a frame-level complex model like the bass ComplexModel for the other voices (the bass gained 0.12 over the power model there), per-note attack transients, and a re-transcription check of the low register where the 4.8 dB error lives.
- **mix, 99.064**, is above 99 but sits on a loudness trade: at the reference loudness under the -1.05 dBTP ceiling it scores 98.84. A transparent multiband or look-ahead limiter fitted to the reference crest factor would let the mix match -9.02 LUFS without the limiter error; the signed mix error is -0.3 to -0.6 dB in every group, the remaining level gap.
- **vocals** depends on V_034 drums, bass and other as leakage components; with the new stems the leakage could be refitted on V_037 stems (IterateVocals `--base V_037`), which may move it a few hundredths either way.
- Measured but not changed: the bass 2 to 6 kHz group (6.3 dB mean, 7 percent of the bass error), the bass note at 2.64 s one octave off.

